WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.088
Why does this module come at the end?

2
00:00:02.088 --> 00:00:05.445
Because every gate before
it ends in a state:

3
00:00:05.445 --> 00:00:08.337
an owner, a target, a credential, a scope.

4
00:00:08.337 --> 00:00:10.376
This module keeps that state true.

5
00:00:10.376 --> 00:00:13.401
A credential added by
hand, a new consent grant,

6
00:00:13.401 --> 00:00:15.789
an app nobody has used in ninety days,

7
00:00:15.789 --> 00:00:20.647
which is Microsoft Learn's threshold
for an unused app, or an owner who left:

8
00:00:20.647 --> 00:00:24.787
each one shows up as drift, against
a baseline someone approved.

9
00:00:24.787 --> 00:00:27.480
Then the evidence has to reach the ISSO in

10
00:00:27.480 --> 00:00:30.251
a form they can trust
without trusting you.

11
00:00:30.251 --> 00:00:35.150
Each run is packaged with a hash for
every file, and chained to the run before.

12
00:00:35.150 --> 00:00:39.363
The ISSO checks a package with
the standard checksum tool alone.

13
00:00:39.363 --> 00:00:43.900
And a period summary shows whether
the checks ran every day, with no gap.
